Subject: [PATCH] dm: repair STA delta removal and association ordering

Implement the empty runtime remove_sta path and free the removed dm_sta_t.
Enforce the non-MLO single-association invariant before inserting the new map
entry, while the stale objects are still available to identify and delete
their database rows. Also build delete_list keys with the required RUID
component.

The previous candidate enforced after update_list; put_sta had already hidden
the stale map entry by then, leaving the old STAList row persistent. Runtime
reproduced two Associated=1 rows after a successful steer.

The single-association rule (same STA id, different BSSID => delete) is correct
only for non-MLO records. An MLO station legitimately associates on multiple
links (different BSSIDs under one MLD), which are not stale, so the enforcement
is gated behind EM_MLO_SUPPORT (undefined by default; an MLO build must compile
it out and add per-MLD/per-link handling). This keeps the invariant from
silently becoming the permanent data model as Wi-Fi 7 / 6 GHz become realistic.

Upstream-Status: Pending
